 analysis of classical texts"},{"text":"Open-access scholarly databases"},{"text":"Cultural knowledge graphs"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future researchers will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Traditional language scholarship","historical methodology","digital humanities","computational tools."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Core Indology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indian history"},{"text":"Indian civilization"},{"text":"Sanskrit"},{"text":"Vedic studies"},{"text":"Indian philosophy"},{"text":"Religious studies"},{"text":"Cultural history"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Philology"},{"text":"Textual criticism"},{"text":"Historiography"},{"text":"Source criticism"},{"text":"Comparative research"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Citation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manuscriptology"},{"text":"Epigraphy"},{"text":"Paleography"},{"text":"Archaeology awareness"},{"text":"Yoga philosophy"},{"text":"Jyotisha studies"},{"text":"Buddhist/Jain studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"Unicode"},{"text":"TEI/XML"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Digital humanities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research presentation"},{"text":"Conference participation"},{"text":"Academic publishing"},{"text":"Grant writing"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Collaboration"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Portfolio Target","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong Sanskrit foundation"},{"text":"Additional classical/regional language where relevant"},{"text":"3–5 primary-text analyses"},{"text":"Sanskrit translation samples"},{"text":"Research methodology project"},{"text":"Manuscript documentation exe